[verification-budget
  [; The verification-cost BOUNDS (#1562, RULED: VCOST-1). The owner's sentence
     — "the fixture grader ≤ 20 min, a selected post-merge run ≤ 20 min, the
     union ≤ 60 min" — has to be a step or it is a wish; #1903 (the owner,
     2026-10-09) moved the union to 20 minutes with every other pre-merge run, and a step needs the
     numbers in one place with the measurement that set each and the issue that
     last moved it.

     A bound moves ONLY in a commit that names why, and never to make a run
     pass: raising one because a run exceeded it is the ratchet running
     backwards, and `check-verification-budget` says so in its own refusal. ]

  [bound name=fixture-grader seconds=1200
    [what 'make fixtures, unselected — the seven grader shards over the whole module corpus']
    [measured '1,384 s census on 2026-09-17; connector.cxd alone 2,898 s under load after #1515 (3,168 s before), which is why the shard split and the shared parse both count toward this row']
    [moved-by 1515]
    [note 'the residue is 260 harness cases waiting out real bounds — 89% of connector.cxd. Lowering this row further is #1515s letter, not a tightening here.']]

  [bound name=selected-run seconds=1200
    [what 'a SELECTED post-merge run — make test-changed BASE=<last passed head> plus the branch steps it selects']
    [measured '817 s on the selected run of 2026-10-04 23:59Z, idle box (load 1.85) — the row the loop wrote; the bound moves DOWN to the owner'"'"'s sentence (20 min) now that an idle run sits under it (#1562, RULED: STREAM-1). Before: 9,263 s, the first row the loop wrote on 884c05469 (2026-09-19), raised to that on the owner'"'"'s word of 2026-09-21']
    [moved-by 1562]
    [note 'ratchets DOWN only from here; the post-merge run as steps (#1817) is the next change to its time.']]

  [bound name=union seconds=1200
    [what 'make test — the whole TEST_TARGETS union, the post-merge run of cx-private (scripts/postmerge_steps.cx)']
    [measured '2,575 s on 715d2262a (2026-10-09 10:53Z, load 9.35 at its start): prebuild 314 + the parallel phase 1,016 (test-vcx-suite 999) + the load-sensitive phase 1,245 (perf-pair 529); 2,738-6,239 s on the eight ticks before it, median about 4,500 s — the rows the loop wrote. Before: 3,600 s (the 60-minute sentence of #1562), 10,516 s on 57745f541 (2026-09-19)']
    [moved-by 1903]
    [note 'the owner 2026-10-09 13:15Z (#1903): the pre-merge run of every repository at or under 20 minutes, the budget enforced by a gate step; judged on the median of the last five runs (check_verification_budget.cx). It reds until the cuts of #1903 land, which is the point. BUDGET-LOAD = (a) (owner 2026-10-10 12:44Z, #1917): only QUIET runs judge, a load at or under 8 (the #1450 bound); a loaded tick is recorded and reported not judged (load N), never red. The bound did not move.']]

  [bound name=premerge-* seconds=1200
    [what 'the pre-merge run of each pinned repository — make deps + make check at its pin with the cx of the tree, one premerge-<repo> row per repository (scripts/premerge_record.sh, make premerge-record)']
    [measured '2026-10-09 15:0xZ, the cx of 715d2262a, load 25-79: every green one under 200 s — cx-platform-flow 199, cx-core-code 44, cx-platform-ux 26, cx-platform-xap 7, the rest under 5 (cx-private#1903)']
    [moved-by 1903]
    [note 'a family: the median of the last five rows of each repository judges on its own. A repository whose check is red records nothing (the stream owns the red), so it reads unmeasured.']]
]
